httpRequests.description:
Creates a timeline and returns it. `visibility`, `showCreator`, `itemSpacing`, the separator sizes and the export background settings use your preferences when left out. So do the `formation` display settings, and students in `formation` get your default level if you have that preference on.

To attach a team, send `formation`, the timeline's own copy of it (`name`, `type`, `rows`, `rowGap`, `displayOverline`, `noDisplayRole`, `groupsVertical`). It's public whenever the timeline is. `formationId` optionally links it to one of your saved formations and is only returned to you. `exportIncludeFormation` sets whether exported images include it by default.

**Raid details**

Optional `raid` tags the timeline: `type` (`Raid`, `EliminateRaid`, `MultiFloorRaid`, `TimeAttackDungeon` or `WorldRaid`), `boss` of that type (the drill type for `TimeAttackDungeon`), `defenseTypes` (which also accept the colors `red`, `yellow`, `blue`, `purple` and `green`), `terrains`, `difficulty` (`Raid` and `EliminateRaid` only), `floor` from 1 to 124 (`MultiFloorRaid` only) and `season` (`id`, `startDate`, `endDate` of a roadmap raid). Send `null` to clear it. `autoName` marks the name as generated by the editor; setting `name` without it turns that off.

